			<item> <title>The Master, 2012</title> <link>https://letterboxd.com/ljstelzer8/film/the-master-2012/</link> <guid isPermaLink="false">letterboxd-review-1010622659</guid> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Sep 2025 03:46:19 +1200</pubDate> <letterboxd:watchedDate>2025-09-10</letterboxd:watchedDate> <letterboxd:rewatch>No</letterboxd:rewatch> <letterboxd:filmTitle>The Master</letterboxd:filmTitle> <letterboxd:filmYear>2012</letterboxd:filmYear> <letterboxd:memberLike>No</letterboxd:memberLike> <tmdb:movieId>68722</tmdb:movieId> <description><![CDATA[ <p><img src="https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/5/2/5/1/2/52512-the-master-2012-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=7cac18ee61"/></p> <p>Another great character study from PTA. This movie shows how people can get tricked into putting their life into something that seems meaningful but is in reality completely meaningless, and how you can lose out on real things in the mean time. Hoffman is also great at playing a cult leader.</p> ]]></description> <dc:creator>ljstelzer8</dc:creator> </item>
		
			<item> <title>Caught Stealing, 2025 - ★★★</title> <link>https://letterboxd.com/ljstelzer8/film/caught-stealing/</link> <guid isPermaLink="false">letterboxd-review-1010621144</guid> <pubDate>Thu, 11 Sep 2025 03:43:32 +1200</pubDate> <letterboxd:watchedDate>2025-09-10</letterboxd:watchedDate> <letterboxd:rewatch>No</letterboxd:rewatch> <letterboxd:filmTitle>Caught Stealing</letterboxd:filmTitle> <letterboxd:filmYear>2025</letterboxd:filmYear> <letterboxd:memberRating>3.0</letterboxd:memberRating> <letterboxd:memberLike>No</letterboxd:memberLike> <tmdb:movieId>1245993</tmdb:movieId> <description><![CDATA[ <p><img src="https://a.ltrbxd.com/resized/film-poster/1/1/2/9/1/9/9/1129199-caught-stealing-0-600-0-900-crop.jpg?v=d3b8da3722"/></p> <p>An entertaining watch, but I have no desire to see it again. Maybe I'm overthinking it but the movie seems kind of confused with its tone, one second it wants me to take Austin Butlers trauma and struggles seriously, and the next it wants me to laugh at his life being totally destroyed. I think this movie could've done better at slowly escalating the chaos throughout the movie as opposed to his life being trashed from like 45 minutes in.</p> ]]></description> <dc:creator>ljstelzer8</dc:creator> </item>
		
